3
00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:17,350
[Your Third Series]

4
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:22,920
Don't forget me.

5
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:26,210
After dealing with everything here,
I'll be on my way to you.

6
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:31,830
Whoa. Not drunk, huh?

7
00:00:31,850 --> 00:00:33,000
Look at you.

8
00:00:36,830 --> 00:00:37,730
- Ugh...
- Mm...

9
00:00:41,230 --> 00:00:42,100
We got soaked in the rain.

10
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:43,160
Go take a shower first.

11
00:00:43,570 --> 00:00:45,760
Let go of me.

12
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:51,280
Sarmonkey should stay in the monkeys' world.

13
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:54,580
Do not stick your nose into ours...

14
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:05,459
Is this how you talk to your senior,

15
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:09,310
JiJi?

16
00:01:21,470 --> 00:01:22,780
Who even is...

17
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:24,570
JiJi?

18
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:27,060
It's you, obviously,

19
00:01:28,380 --> 00:01:29,380
"Ji"ranat.

20
00:01:34,090 --> 00:01:35,780
My name is Jam,

21
00:01:36,759 --> 00:01:37,979
not "Snoop,"

22
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:41,470
"JiJi," or whatever you just called me.

23
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:45,250
Please get it right,

24
00:01:46,330 --> 00:01:48,570
or else I will report you
to the authorities.

25
00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:57,580
All you do is tease me.

26
00:01:58,460 --> 00:01:59,950
Is it really that much fun?

27
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:03,460
Can I do the same to you

28
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,770
so you know how bad it feels?

29
00:02:09,389 --> 00:02:10,860
When did I ever do
anything like that to you?

30
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:12,980
Hm?

31
00:03:05,990 --> 00:03:07,460
Like this.

32
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:04,850
Go ahead.

33
00:04:08,890 --> 00:04:10,360
Tease me however you like.

34
00:04:13,070 --> 00:04:14,070
Right now,

35
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:18,279
I'm but a little chick in your hands.

36
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:35,490
[Your Third Series]

37
00:04:45,980 --> 00:04:49,909
♫Still feeling lonely? Well, you've got me,♫

38
00:04:49,950 --> 00:04:54,390
♫Keeping you busy every day♫

39
00:04:55,110 --> 00:04:59,050
♫I might not be the one you wanted,♫

40
00:04:59,110 --> 00:05:03,810
♫But give it time, you'll love me anyway♫

41
00:05:04,260 --> 00:05:08,790
♫It's your heart, so it's your choice,♫

42
00:05:08,810 --> 00:05:13,250
♫I won't ever stand in your way♫

43
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:17,640
♫But when they make you blue,♫

44
00:05:17,690 --> 00:05:21,400
♫Can you please let me take care of you?♫

45
00:05:22,370 --> 00:05:27,040
♫I'm here to love you as myself,
not as a surrogate♫

46
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:30,830
♫Let me be your safe space
when you need a break♫

47
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:35,850
♫Who cares if I'm not your first or second?♫

48
00:05:35,930 --> 00:05:40,400
♫At least being your third still counts♫

49
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:45,350
♫I'm here to love you,
no matter who left you with heartache♫

50
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:49,060
♫Just let me heal your heart,
lending you my aid♫

51
00:05:49,090 --> 00:05:54,200
♫Have faith and believe in love once more♫

52
00:05:54,230 --> 00:05:56,210
♫'Cause good love is your Lucky Third♫

53
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:59,440
♫Your Third, can it be me, love?♫

54
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:02,020
[Your Third Series]

55
00:09:45,410 --> 00:09:46,920
Aren't you gonna put some clothes on first?

56
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:49,470
I would rather not.

57
00:09:50,690 --> 00:09:52,500
This is fine just the way it is.

58
00:09:55,590 --> 00:09:56,680
Are you sober now?

59
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,490
Yes, from the start.

60
00:10:17,270 --> 00:10:18,880
Aren't you uncomfortable?

61
00:10:25,290 --> 00:10:26,780
You take it off, too.

62
00:11:18,230 --> 00:11:19,590
Are we just going to sleep,

63
00:11:21,920 --> 00:11:22,800
or...

64
00:11:28,550 --> 00:11:29,550
are you going to be mine?

65
00:12:21,060 --> 00:12:22,060
Can I have you?

66
00:13:30,620 --> 00:13:31,380
Jam.

67
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:33,520
Jam.

68
00:13:34,970 --> 00:13:35,700
Jam.

69
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:38,940
Jam...

70
00:13:41,770 --> 00:13:42,850
Jam.

71
00:13:44,690 --> 00:13:45,260
Jam!

72
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:46,680
Jam!

73
00:13:47,070 --> 00:13:48,030
Jam!!

74
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:49,180
Jam!

75
00:13:50,230 --> 00:13:50,800
Jam!!

76
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:52,050
Jam!

77
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:52,670
Jam!!

78
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:57,810
Jam...

79
00:13:58,910 --> 00:13:59,890
Jam...

80
00:14:01,930 --> 00:14:03,410
Why is he avoiding me?

81
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:04,910
Did I go too far last night?

82
00:14:05,570 --> 00:14:07,370
I shouldn't have let my feelings
take hold of me.

83
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:15,200
Jam...

84
00:14:43,570 --> 00:14:44,730
Juju.

85
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:49,230
Juju.

86
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:56,770
After returning home...

87
00:14:57,290 --> 00:14:59,170
the first order of business
is to call Mr. Sib

88
00:14:59,890 --> 00:15:03,070
and tell him that the mission to
Hunt Down the Teeny-tiny Tiger has failed.

89
00:15:17,790 --> 00:15:18,880
Hello, Mr. Sib.

90
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:20,070
Mr. Jam.

91
00:15:20,110 --> 00:15:21,110
Perfect timing.

92
00:15:21,370 --> 00:15:22,370
You're back, aren't you?

93
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:25,360
Yes.

94
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:29,480
I am calling you to talk about this matter,

95
00:15:31,810 --> 00:15:33,880
and I also have a request.

96
00:15:35,090 --> 00:15:36,020
What is it?

97
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,480
I'm currently in Pak Chong.

98
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:39,280
How about we talk here?

99
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:41,110
I also have something
I want to talk to you about.

100
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:43,470
I'd like you to come support Song.

101
00:15:43,510 --> 00:15:45,130
He's a bit tied up.

102
00:15:45,190 --> 00:15:46,000
No problem.

103
00:15:46,190 --> 00:15:47,480
I will be there right away.

104
00:15:47,640 --> 00:15:48,270
Right.

105
00:15:58,860 --> 00:16:00,790
We just saw each other,

106
00:16:01,740 --> 00:16:03,810
and now we have to be apart again, Juju...

107
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:25,780
"I love my job."

108
00:16:26,250 --> 00:16:27,610
"I love my job."

109
00:16:28,090 --> 00:16:29,060
"I love my job."

110
00:16:29,670 --> 00:16:31,140
"I love my job..."

111
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:32,260
"I love my job..."

112
00:16:32,450 --> 00:16:33,370
"I love my job."

113
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:34,480
- Oh!
- Oh, good heavens!

114
00:16:35,090 --> 00:16:35,940
Jam...

115
00:16:36,190 --> 00:16:36,820
Song...

116
00:16:36,940 --> 00:16:37,970
Hello.

117
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:38,850
Hi.

118
00:16:38,900 --> 00:16:40,280
Uh... Are you okay?

119
00:16:40,650 --> 00:16:41,340
Oh...

120
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:43,270
Are you hurt?
I bumped into you pretty hard...

121
00:16:43,310 --> 00:16:44,270
I am fine.

122
00:16:44,310 --> 00:16:45,100
It was nothing.

123
00:16:45,130 --> 00:16:46,360
Okay.

124
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:50,540
Let me go get some snacks first.

125
00:16:50,740 --> 00:16:52,290
Oh, snacks...

126
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:53,380
At the cafe?

127
00:16:54,470 --> 00:16:55,390
Yes.

128
00:16:56,110 --> 00:16:56,640
Well, then...

129
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:58,380
Let me treat you to them

130
00:16:58,670 --> 00:16:59,890
as an apology.

131
00:17:11,490 --> 00:17:12,700
And where's Sarm?

132
00:17:15,130 --> 00:17:16,569
Well...

133
00:17:20,450 --> 00:17:21,480
"Don't forget me."

134
00:17:21,510 --> 00:17:23,780
"After dealing with everything here,
I'll be on my way to you."

135
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:26,680
It's okay.

136
00:17:28,010 --> 00:17:29,400
You did your best, Jam.

137
00:17:30,790 --> 00:17:32,090
Let's set that matter aside

138
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:33,510
and...

139
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:35,670
talk about what's going on now.

140
00:17:37,380 --> 00:17:38,790
Come with me, then, will you?

141
00:17:39,590 --> 00:17:40,450
I need your help.

142
00:17:42,530 --> 00:17:42,950
Right.

143
00:17:51,020 --> 00:17:52,630
If something is troubling you,

144
00:17:52,750 --> 00:17:54,290
you can share it with me, Song.

145
00:17:55,190 --> 00:17:56,070
Isn't a wedding

146
00:17:56,100 --> 00:17:58,220
supposed to be about just two people?

147
00:17:58,250 --> 00:17:58,900
You see,

148
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,370
the more people we invite,

149
00:18:00,590 --> 00:18:02,090
the busier things get,

150
00:18:02,130 --> 00:18:03,510
and the more problems arise,

151
00:18:03,610 --> 00:18:04,610
with the latest being that

152
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:07,800
the flower bouquet
the groom needs this evening

153
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:09,830
has yet to arrive.

154
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:11,260
Where is it being shipped from?

155
00:18:11,370 --> 00:18:12,370
Switzerland.

156
00:18:12,970 --> 00:18:15,180
Then allow me to check for you and see

157
00:18:15,390 --> 00:18:17,140
if the flower bouquet arrived on the flight.

158
00:18:17,350 --> 00:18:18,310
I will try contacting

159
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:20,580
the air freight department directly.

160
00:18:20,930 --> 00:18:21,490
Oh.

161
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:23,590
I'll leave you to it, then.

162
00:18:24,270 --> 00:18:25,700
You handle it.

163
00:18:25,850 --> 00:18:27,190
I'll support you.

164
00:18:27,860 --> 00:18:28,860
Okay.

165
00:18:29,830 --> 00:18:30,490
Thank you.

166
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:34,990
All done.

167
00:18:35,590 --> 00:18:37,460
They informed us that
they would look into it urgently

168
00:18:37,530 --> 00:18:40,270
and reply via email within half an hour.

169
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:43,220
Thank you very much, Jam.

170
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:45,780
Take it easy, Song.

171
00:18:46,470 --> 00:18:47,670
Every solution

172
00:18:47,820 --> 00:18:49,010
has a problem.

173
00:18:49,940 --> 00:18:50,640
The other way around.

174
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:53,850
Of course.

175
00:18:54,230 --> 00:18:54,790
Let's go.

176
00:18:57,660 --> 00:18:58,580
Jam.

177
00:18:58,620 --> 00:18:59,670
Thank you, Song.

178
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:02,210
Let's go.

179
00:19:57,660 --> 00:19:58,270
Dad.

180
00:19:59,250 --> 00:19:59,830
Mm.

181
00:20:00,030 --> 00:20:00,720
Hello.

182
00:20:00,750 --> 00:20:01,360
Right.

183
00:20:05,010 --> 00:20:06,330
"This wounded tiger..."

184
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:07,230
Hmph.

185
00:20:07,710 --> 00:20:10,490
"I will return when I am fine."

186
00:20:11,840 --> 00:20:13,900
So you came back because you're fine now?

187
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:15,100
Dad,

188
00:20:15,270 --> 00:20:16,540
go easy on me.

189
00:20:16,650 --> 00:20:17,980
Where's the bride of the hour?

190
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:19,770
And where are the others?

191
00:20:19,810 --> 00:20:20,570
Where did they go?

192
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:24,180
Namnueng is taking care of tonight's event
at the reception hall.

193
00:20:24,620 --> 00:20:26,770
Song is taking care of the venue.

194
00:20:26,910 --> 00:20:28,570
Sib and PiMai

195
00:20:28,750 --> 00:20:30,240
are taking care of the guests for me.

196
00:20:32,120 --> 00:20:32,950
And Mom?

197
00:20:33,700 --> 00:20:34,390
Is she coming?

198
00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:38,020
It's our daughter's wedding,
for goodness' sake.

199
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:40,470
There's no way she'd miss it.

200
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:44,980
Dad, Mom wants you to know that...

201
00:20:46,790 --> 00:20:47,790
Sarm!

202
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:49,240
Sarm!

203
00:20:51,820 --> 00:20:53,680
I thought you weren't coming back.

204
00:20:54,300 --> 00:20:55,540
I have to be here, don't I?

205
00:20:56,100 --> 00:20:57,470
This is my home, too.

206
00:20:59,140 --> 00:21:00,140
Namnueng.

207
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:01,930
Wow.

208
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:03,250
You're on fire!

209
00:21:03,280 --> 00:21:04,000
Like, fabulous!

210
00:21:04,030 --> 00:21:05,200
You're shining brilliantly.

211
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:06,180
Let me tell you this.

212
00:21:06,210 --> 00:21:07,510
If I put you up against the stars,

213
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:09,700
you'd outshine all of them.

214
00:21:09,730 --> 00:21:10,670
Enough already.

215
00:21:11,280 --> 00:21:13,160
Get dressed up, will you?

216
00:21:13,690 --> 00:21:15,860
I thought the suit I had tailored
would be collecting dust.

217
00:21:15,890 --> 00:21:16,750
Wait.

218
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:18,950
Who got fitted for the suit instead of me?

219
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:19,530
Oh.

220
00:21:19,750 --> 00:21:20,500
It was Sib.

221
00:21:20,850 --> 00:21:23,020
You two are just about the same size.

222
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:24,870
Gosh, how could you compare me to him?

223
00:21:24,910 --> 00:21:25,560
I am

224
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:26,600
bigger

225
00:21:26,630 --> 00:21:28,840
and longer

226
00:21:28,890 --> 00:21:29,620
by a mile!

227
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:34,060
When it comes to this kind of stuff...

228
00:21:34,090 --> 00:21:35,040
Just look at the door.

229
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:35,680
- There.
- Why?

230
00:21:35,710 --> 00:21:36,330
Mine is this big,

231
00:21:36,360 --> 00:21:37,730
and it can reach that door from here.

232
00:21:37,770 --> 00:21:39,500
The apple doesn't fall far from the tree.

233
00:21:39,770 --> 00:21:42,020
We both have it,
but you're totally outclassed!

234
00:21:42,450 --> 00:21:44,380
Gosh, enough, both of you.

235
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:46,520
Sarm, get dressed up already.

236
00:21:46,560 --> 00:21:48,220
Come on, the guests are waiting, Sarm.

237
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:49,580
- Alright.
- Come on.

238
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:39,380
My eyes must have played tricks on me.

239
00:22:40,420 --> 00:22:42,680
Mr. Sarm is still on Ko Pha-ngan, is he?

240
00:23:02,270 --> 00:23:03,420
So gorgeous.

241
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:04,880
Thank you.

242
00:23:14,900 --> 00:23:16,180
How could this night go on without me?

243
00:23:30,720 --> 00:23:31,980
I know I'm handsome,

244
00:23:32,600 --> 00:23:34,430
but you don't have to
stare at me so much, do you?

245
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:35,690
Mm.

246
00:23:36,350 --> 00:23:37,300
He got it from me.

247
00:23:37,570 --> 00:23:38,280
Hm?

248
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:39,900
And his father.

249
00:23:39,930 --> 00:23:40,880
Oh.

250
00:23:41,220 --> 00:23:42,380
- That's true.
- Mm.

251
00:23:42,860 --> 00:23:43,950
And his older sister.

252
00:23:43,980 --> 00:23:44,700
Yes.

253
00:23:44,830 --> 00:23:46,220
It's three to one. What about it?

254
00:23:46,540 --> 00:23:47,230
Sarm.

255
00:23:47,260 --> 00:23:48,020
Hm?

256
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:49,760
Did you hear that?

257
00:23:49,790 --> 00:23:50,120
Hear what?

258
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:52,740
What's gotten into our dad and siblings?

259
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:55,200
It's probably love.

260
00:23:55,650 --> 00:23:57,200
Get used to it.

261
00:23:57,260 --> 00:23:57,960
Tonight,

262
00:23:58,250 --> 00:23:59,580
you've got plenty more surprises

263
00:23:59,660 --> 00:24:00,660
coming your way.

264
00:24:01,700 --> 00:24:02,360
Sarm.

265
00:24:03,360 --> 00:24:05,460
Don't run off anywhere
after tonight's over, okay?

266
00:24:05,700 --> 00:24:06,740
I've got something to talk to you about.

267
00:24:07,060 --> 00:24:07,740
Don't boss me around.

268
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:09,870
Why can't I?

269
00:24:10,570 --> 00:24:11,660
There's only one person

270
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:12,740
who has that power.

271
00:24:13,410 --> 00:24:13,980
Who?

272
00:24:14,010 --> 00:24:15,060
Dad, obviously.

273
00:24:15,830 --> 00:24:16,540
Whoa, incredible.

274
00:24:16,580 --> 00:24:17,580
- My son.
- You heard me.

275
00:24:17,610 --> 00:24:18,520
Yes, of course.

276
00:24:18,550 --> 00:24:19,570
He said it himself.

277
00:24:19,610 --> 00:24:21,440
I'm the one who can boss him around.

278
00:24:21,470 --> 00:24:21,960
Understood?

279
00:24:22,250 --> 00:24:23,380
But I'm your son, too, Dad.

280
00:24:23,410 --> 00:24:24,720
Hey, he's my son, you hear?

281
00:24:24,760 --> 00:24:25,810
- Huh?
- Want to pick a fight?

282
00:24:25,860 --> 00:24:27,140
Hey, but I'm your younger brother.

283
00:24:27,290 --> 00:24:28,100
Want a piece of this?

284
00:24:28,350 --> 00:24:28,830
And he's my brother.

285
00:24:28,860 --> 00:24:30,210
Whoa, and that makes two.

286
00:24:30,260 --> 00:24:31,190
I don't care.

287
00:24:31,490 --> 00:24:32,780
I'm the boss here.

288
00:24:33,210 --> 00:24:34,210
Hey, wait.

289
00:24:34,300 --> 00:24:35,300
You want to talk to him?

290
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:35,960
About what?

291
00:24:36,020 --> 00:24:37,590
Finding him a beauty queen?

292
00:24:37,710 --> 00:24:39,370
Let me tell you, his partner

293
00:24:39,710 --> 00:24:40,890
must be a badass.

294
00:24:42,290 --> 00:24:43,980
The kind with total devastation, Dad?

295
00:24:44,050 --> 00:24:45,180
That's old news.

296
00:24:45,270 --> 00:24:46,100
Now, it has to be

297
00:24:46,140 --> 00:24:47,700
"with total annihilation."

298
00:24:47,730 --> 00:24:48,320
Clear?

299
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:49,360
Oh, that's wonderful.

300
00:24:49,970 --> 00:24:50,710
Hey.

301
00:24:51,030 --> 00:24:52,190
Dad, don't tell me

302
00:24:52,230 --> 00:24:53,930
you're finding Sarm a partner,

303
00:24:53,960 --> 00:24:56,010
like how you matched Sib with PiMai?

304
00:24:56,470 --> 00:24:57,930
Oh, these two

305
00:24:58,310 --> 00:24:59,180
love each other,

306
00:24:59,200 --> 00:25:00,390
but they didn't even know it,

307
00:25:00,630 --> 00:25:01,290
alright?

308
00:25:06,300 --> 00:25:07,230
Exactly.

309
00:25:07,430 --> 00:25:08,270
We love each other.

310
00:25:10,020 --> 00:25:11,110
Oh, how about that?

311
00:25:12,350 --> 00:25:13,300
See what I mean?

312
00:25:13,380 --> 00:25:14,250
How about that?

313
00:25:14,350 --> 00:25:15,430
They're hammering it home,

314
00:25:15,830 --> 00:25:16,310
aren't they?

315
00:25:16,340 --> 00:25:17,160
Hammer it home.

316
00:25:17,250 --> 00:25:18,320
Oh, my, that's a good one.

317
00:25:18,350 --> 00:25:19,030
How about that?

318
00:25:19,070 --> 00:25:19,670
How about that?

319
00:25:19,710 --> 00:25:20,760
Oh, so,

320
00:25:20,790 --> 00:25:22,050
you're playing the role

321
00:25:22,070 --> 00:25:25,250
of a kind-hearted cupid,
aren't you, Mr. Decha?

322
00:25:25,280 --> 00:25:26,280
Hm?

323
00:25:30,610 --> 00:25:31,350
Well then,

324
00:25:31,610 --> 00:25:32,790
I'll head inside.

325
00:25:32,850 --> 00:25:33,640
- Mm.
- Right.

326
00:25:33,670 --> 00:25:34,420
See you there.

327
00:25:34,450 --> 00:25:34,890
Okay.

328
00:25:34,920 --> 00:25:35,570
Wait.

329
00:25:35,610 --> 00:25:36,310
I'm coming with you.

330
00:25:36,570 --> 00:25:37,460
- See you.
- Mm.

331
00:25:38,060 --> 00:25:39,060
- Come on.
- This way.

332
00:25:42,310 --> 00:25:43,310
Let me look at you.

333
00:25:43,580 --> 00:25:44,740
- Whoa.
- Do I look beautiful?

334
00:25:44,780 --> 00:25:46,930
You're as beautiful as an angel,

335
00:25:47,150 --> 00:25:47,660
my daughter.

336
00:25:48,110 --> 00:25:48,680
Come on.

337
00:25:59,530 --> 00:26:00,400
Jam.

338
00:26:01,750 --> 00:26:02,810
Song.

339
00:26:03,290 --> 00:26:04,320
Is everything okay?

340
00:26:06,380 --> 00:26:07,520
All is going well.

341
00:26:09,910 --> 00:26:11,150
Whoa.

342
00:26:11,910 --> 00:26:13,370
You look wonderful, Song.

343
00:26:13,890 --> 00:26:16,150
You're making me blush
with that compliment, Jam.

344
00:26:16,740 --> 00:26:17,490
But...

345
00:26:17,840 --> 00:26:19,170
I still haven't showered.

346
00:26:19,480 --> 00:26:21,050
Is that so, Song?

347
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:22,610
Please keep this between us.

348
00:26:23,810 --> 00:26:24,730
Okay.

349
00:26:26,820 --> 00:26:28,110
I will keep this a secret

350
00:26:28,150 --> 00:26:29,210
between us.

351
00:26:29,570 --> 00:26:30,490
Thank you.

352
00:26:35,690 --> 00:26:36,820
Oh, Little Jam.

353
00:26:37,340 --> 00:26:38,110
Where are you?

354
00:26:38,720 --> 00:26:39,320
Oh.

355
00:26:39,750 --> 00:26:40,600
Dear Traiphop.

356
00:26:41,310 --> 00:26:41,950
Oh,

357
00:26:42,120 --> 00:26:43,010
Uncle Kraisorn.

358
00:26:43,070 --> 00:26:43,540
Good evening.

359
00:26:43,580 --> 00:26:44,390
Good evening.

360
00:26:44,580 --> 00:26:47,080
You've been gone a long time, haven't you?

361
00:26:47,170 --> 00:26:47,910
How are things?

362
00:26:47,950 --> 00:26:49,040
It's been so long.

363
00:26:49,080 --> 00:26:51,340
You look a lot more buff than before, too.

364
00:26:51,400 --> 00:26:52,090
Whoa...

365
00:26:52,120 --> 00:26:53,230
I wouldn't say that.

366
00:26:53,610 --> 00:26:54,470
What about you, Uncle?

367
00:26:54,510 --> 00:26:55,380
Have you been doing well?

368
00:26:55,410 --> 00:26:57,170
As usual, for an old man.

369
00:26:57,250 --> 00:26:57,800
Oh,

370
00:26:58,010 --> 00:27:00,310
I brought him here for you

371
00:27:00,350 --> 00:27:01,460
to look after.

372
00:27:01,600 --> 00:27:03,600
He's been working at Adisuan Farm

373
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:05,290
for just over a month.

374
00:27:09,950 --> 00:27:11,020
You're Ning-nong, right?

375
00:27:12,710 --> 00:27:13,290
Yes.

376
00:27:13,660 --> 00:27:14,620
Good evening, Mr. Sarm.

377
00:27:15,350 --> 00:27:16,540
No need to call me "Mr. Sarm."

378
00:27:16,570 --> 00:27:17,430
Just call me by my name.

379
00:27:21,140 --> 00:27:22,240
How did you end up working here?

380
00:27:22,620 --> 00:27:24,310
Uh... I just graduated.

381
00:27:24,840 --> 00:27:26,720
And I noticed that your farm, Mr. Sarm...

382
00:27:27,080 --> 00:27:28,610
Uhh... I mean, Sarm...

383
00:27:28,780 --> 00:27:30,070
You were looking for a vet,

384
00:27:30,100 --> 00:27:31,830
so I quickly applied for that position

385
00:27:32,130 --> 00:27:34,180
because I've been wanting to work here
since I was little.

386
00:27:34,330 --> 00:27:35,690
Whoa...

387
00:27:36,230 --> 00:27:37,080
You know how to talk, huh?

388
00:27:37,760 --> 00:27:38,410
Right.

389
00:27:38,450 --> 00:27:39,220
Okay.

390
00:27:39,250 --> 00:27:40,000
Here.

391
00:27:41,040 --> 00:27:42,500
You can always call me
if you need anything.

392
00:27:42,710 --> 00:27:43,890
Don't hesitate.

393
00:27:44,110 --> 00:27:44,890
Your number.

394
00:27:46,080 --> 00:27:47,310
And don't worry, Uncle.

395
00:27:47,350 --> 00:27:48,260
I'll take care of him.

396
00:27:48,300 --> 00:27:49,210
Whoa.

397
00:27:49,340 --> 00:27:51,810
That puts my mind at ease.

398
00:27:51,980 --> 00:27:53,320
You two get close, okay?

399
00:27:53,410 --> 00:27:54,390
Absolutely.

400
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:56,720
Feel free to call me whenever.

401
00:27:57,380 --> 00:27:58,040
Thank you, Uncle.

402
00:27:58,070 --> 00:27:59,020
- I have to go now.
- Right.

403
00:27:59,050 --> 00:27:59,820
- Right.
- Make yourself at home.

404
00:27:59,860 --> 00:28:01,350
- Right.
- Enjoy yourselves.

405
00:28:02,200 --> 00:28:04,000
Work hard, alright?

406
00:28:04,520 --> 00:28:06,030
Take him as an example.

407
00:28:24,840 --> 00:28:27,500
I heard from the main house
that you're back.

408
00:28:29,510 --> 00:28:31,210
At first, it was quite hard to believe.

409
00:28:33,320 --> 00:28:35,030
But seeing you here with my own eyes...

410
00:28:36,660 --> 00:28:38,310
It's clear that you really are.

411
00:28:42,160 --> 00:28:43,310
I couldn't believe it.

412
00:28:46,840 --> 00:28:48,120
You're safe and sound, aren't you?

413
00:28:49,690 --> 00:28:51,180
You're totally fine?

414
00:28:54,910 --> 00:28:56,100
What do you want to happen to me?

415
00:28:57,010 --> 00:28:58,010
You're right.

416
00:29:00,110 --> 00:29:02,160
I thought you'd be gone...

417
00:29:02,200 --> 00:29:03,800
forever.

418
00:29:06,960 --> 00:29:07,910
This is my home.

419
00:29:08,820 --> 00:29:10,690
Sooner or later,
I'll have to come back here.

420
00:29:13,320 --> 00:29:14,920
There's no place like home, right?

421
00:29:15,850 --> 00:29:17,800
Even Ko Pha-ngan can't beat it.

422
00:29:20,130 --> 00:29:21,130
I've only been away for six months,

423
00:29:22,780 --> 00:29:23,880
so there's a lot to catch up on.

424
00:29:25,420 --> 00:29:26,610
We'll talk later.

425
00:29:26,720 --> 00:29:27,720
I need to go now.

426
00:29:28,620 --> 00:29:29,460
Sure thing.

427
00:29:31,790 --> 00:29:33,810
I'm always available for you.

428
00:29:35,210 --> 00:29:36,910
For Adisuan,

429
00:29:37,750 --> 00:29:39,290
I can do anything.

430
00:30:15,210 --> 00:30:16,320
Oh, Jam.

431
00:30:17,550 --> 00:30:18,800
Have you eaten yet?

432
00:30:19,440 --> 00:30:21,710
I think you should go inside
and grab something.

433
00:30:24,190 --> 00:30:25,740
I am not that hungry.

434
00:30:25,910 --> 00:30:27,800
Even if you're not,
you need to have something,

435
00:30:28,110 --> 00:30:30,280
or else...you won't have the energy.

436
00:30:30,600 --> 00:30:32,210
Thank you, Song.

437
00:30:33,130 --> 00:30:35,130
I'm the one who owes you a thank you.

438
00:30:35,520 --> 00:30:36,690
Without you,

439
00:30:36,730 --> 00:30:37,530
I'd be screwed

440
00:30:37,720 --> 00:30:38,720
right now.

441
00:30:39,240 --> 00:30:40,030
Let's...

442
00:30:40,380 --> 00:30:41,610
work together again sometime.

443
00:30:42,170 --> 00:30:44,610
If Mr. Sib sends for me, I will come.

444
00:30:45,900 --> 00:30:48,130
By the way, the next wedding...

445
00:30:49,520 --> 00:30:51,130
is it yours?

446
00:30:52,900 --> 00:30:54,410
My soulmate hasn't been born yet.

447
00:30:54,730 --> 00:30:55,520
But...

448
00:30:55,620 --> 00:30:58,440
the good old feng shui master told me that

449
00:30:58,620 --> 00:30:59,470
an auspicious ceremony

450
00:30:59,500 --> 00:31:00,800
is coming up soon.

451
00:31:01,750 --> 00:31:04,560
If so, I would come bug you
first thing in the morning.

452
00:31:05,300 --> 00:31:06,310
That's a deal, then.

453
00:31:06,740 --> 00:31:08,230
- Deal.
- Deal.

454
00:31:10,430 --> 00:31:12,170
I'll go check on things at the venue first.

455
00:31:12,220 --> 00:31:13,910
Feel free to enjoy yourself.

456
00:31:14,130 --> 00:31:14,930
I'll handle it myself.

457
00:31:14,960 --> 00:31:16,090
Right, Song.

458
00:31:16,450 --> 00:31:17,910
- See you.
- See you.

459
00:31:23,890 --> 00:31:24,850
Mr. Sib.

460
00:31:25,450 --> 00:31:26,300
Oh, Jam.

461
00:31:27,110 --> 00:31:28,530
Has everyone checked in okay?

462
00:31:29,020 --> 00:31:30,100
There is Mr. Autthakorn,

463
00:31:30,130 --> 00:31:32,190
Chairman of
the Eastern Agricultural Association,

464
00:31:32,220 --> 00:31:32,850
and Mr. Maekmai.

465
00:31:32,950 --> 00:31:35,110
They have informed Song that
they are on their way.

466
00:31:35,310 --> 00:31:37,240
Aside from them,
all the other guests are here.

467
00:31:37,350 --> 00:31:38,350
Earlier,

468
00:31:38,380 --> 00:31:40,310
some reporters
tried to blend in with the guests

469
00:31:40,340 --> 00:31:41,300
and get up close.

470
00:31:41,330 --> 00:31:43,110
Song let them go,

471
00:31:43,580 --> 00:31:46,350
but an official warning
will be issued to their media outlet.

472
00:31:46,440 --> 00:31:48,130
They were local journalists.

473
00:31:48,420 --> 00:31:50,570
Are there any other
problematic media outlets?

474
00:31:50,660 --> 00:31:51,370
None.

475
00:31:52,110 --> 00:31:54,490
All media outlets are operating
within our established boundaries.

476
00:31:54,530 --> 00:31:55,610
Everything's going well?

477
00:31:55,780 --> 00:31:57,290
Yes, smoothly.

478
00:32:01,110 --> 00:32:02,110
And...

479
00:32:02,140 --> 00:32:03,240
Have you had anything?

480
00:32:03,390 --> 00:32:05,530
The chef informed me that
there is sufficient food.

481
00:32:05,560 --> 00:32:07,450
However, appetizers

482
00:32:07,490 --> 00:32:09,700
and cocktails will need to be
replenished regularly.

483
00:32:12,650 --> 00:32:14,890
What was the question again, Mr. Sib?

484
00:32:17,620 --> 00:32:18,570
Are you alright?

485
00:32:18,610 --> 00:32:19,280
Yes, Chef!

486
00:32:19,310 --> 00:32:20,190
Wait!

487
00:32:23,270 --> 00:32:24,650
I don't think you are.

488
00:32:26,400 --> 00:32:27,690
I've arranged a house for you.

489
00:32:27,740 --> 00:32:29,170
The house number is right here.

490
00:32:29,540 --> 00:32:31,530
I think...I should go home.

491
00:32:31,570 --> 00:32:32,370
Bad idea.

492
00:32:32,830 --> 00:32:34,210
It's already late. It's too risky.

493
00:32:34,690 --> 00:32:35,600
More importantly,

494
00:32:35,630 --> 00:32:36,370
you and I

495
00:32:36,920 --> 00:32:38,280
have something to discuss.

496
00:32:38,510 --> 00:32:40,010
Tomorrow will be the perfect opportunity.

497
00:32:40,430 --> 00:32:41,120
Here.

498
00:32:41,320 --> 00:32:43,030
You can order food
using the number on the back.

499
00:32:43,560 --> 00:32:45,000
And if you need anything else,

500
00:32:45,030 --> 00:32:46,200
simply inform the staff

501
00:32:46,400 --> 00:32:47,680
and tell them to put my name down.

502
00:32:48,060 --> 00:32:50,010
And feel free to call me anytime.

503
00:32:51,870 --> 00:32:53,010
Yes, Mr. Sib.

504
00:32:56,210 --> 00:32:57,110
Mr. Jam.

505
00:32:57,610 --> 00:32:59,610
You've been doing an excellent job.

506
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:01,300
Go get some rest.

507
00:33:01,560 --> 00:33:02,610
Thank you very much.

508
00:33:03,910 --> 00:33:04,910
Yes, Mr. Sib.

509
00:33:05,830 --> 00:33:06,940
Don't forget to eat.

510
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:54,230
Mr. Sarm...

511
00:34:07,250 --> 00:34:08,040
You stubborn kid.

512
00:34:08,630 --> 00:34:09,630
Come here.

513
00:34:17,500 --> 00:34:18,179
Here.

514
00:36:36,480 --> 00:36:37,480
Mr. Sarm.

515
00:36:37,520 --> 00:36:37,980
Yes?

516
00:36:38,010 --> 00:36:40,390
I've heard from the main house
about your return.

517
00:36:40,430 --> 00:36:41,250
If necessary,

518
00:36:41,280 --> 00:36:43,920
please let me bring six more housekeepers.

519
00:36:44,110 --> 00:36:45,800
While you were away,

520
00:36:45,850 --> 00:36:48,090
they'd been working at the main house.

521
00:36:48,210 --> 00:36:49,620
Why so many, Auntie?

522
00:36:50,030 --> 00:36:51,400
Are we having a sports day here?

523
00:36:51,940 --> 00:36:53,380
Oh, Mr. Sarm...

524
00:36:53,840 --> 00:36:55,980
I simply want to ask

525
00:36:56,010 --> 00:36:58,840
who you'd like to
take care of the housekeeping here.

526
00:36:59,280 --> 00:37:00,580
Anyone will do, Auntie.

527
00:37:00,620 --> 00:37:02,100
Whoever you think is best.

528
00:37:03,150 --> 00:37:04,060
If so,

529
00:37:04,090 --> 00:37:05,500
I'd like Sak's family

530
00:37:05,530 --> 00:37:07,700
to move into the guest house tonight.

531
00:37:07,730 --> 00:37:08,380
Right.

532
00:37:09,100 --> 00:37:09,800
Auntie.

533
00:37:10,620 --> 00:37:12,000
Mr. Jam is staying in the room.

534
00:37:12,360 --> 00:37:13,490
If he wakes up,

535
00:37:13,520 --> 00:37:14,720
please call me, okay?

536
00:37:15,510 --> 00:37:16,510
Mr. Jam?

537
00:37:16,810 --> 00:37:18,210
Who is he?

538
00:37:21,500 --> 00:37:22,900
This feeling I'm having right now..

539
00:37:23,670 --> 00:37:25,710
I'm scared to define what it is.

540
00:37:26,210 --> 00:37:27,450
Despite that,

541
00:37:27,480 --> 00:37:29,910
something deep inside me tells me that

542
00:37:30,900 --> 00:37:32,400
I can't live without Jam.

543
00:37:32,630 --> 00:37:33,920
He's like air,

544
00:37:34,310 --> 00:37:35,420
something I can't live without,

545
00:37:36,410 --> 00:37:37,710
and I need to breathe every day.

546
00:37:42,050 --> 00:37:42,810
I'll be going now.

547
00:37:47,300 --> 00:37:49,400
What did he mean even by "air"?

548
00:37:50,290 --> 00:37:51,250
This old auntie is confused.

549
00:38:00,550 --> 00:38:01,130
Oh.

550
00:38:01,410 --> 00:38:02,190
Sarm.

551
00:38:02,510 --> 00:38:03,510
Where have you been?

552
00:38:05,010 --> 00:38:05,660
Song.

553
00:38:05,820 --> 00:38:07,370
Both of us could use some distance.

554
00:38:08,230 --> 00:38:09,030
What do you mean?

555
00:38:09,520 --> 00:38:10,350
Oh.

556
00:38:10,690 --> 00:38:11,300
PiMai.

557
00:38:11,860 --> 00:38:13,000
PiMai, this way.

558
00:38:13,120 --> 00:38:14,300
Yoo-hoo.

559
00:38:14,330 --> 00:38:15,790
- Song. Sarm.
- This way.

560
00:38:16,060 --> 00:38:16,930
That's right.

561
00:38:16,960 --> 00:38:17,810
PiMai,

562
00:38:17,850 --> 00:38:19,050
come chat with us.

563
00:38:19,080 --> 00:38:19,570
Mm.

564
00:38:19,610 --> 00:38:20,850
Spending all day with Sib

565
00:38:21,010 --> 00:38:21,840
is just boring.

566
00:38:21,870 --> 00:38:23,090
I know, right?

567
00:38:24,060 --> 00:38:25,870
How are you doing, PiMai?

568
00:38:25,910 --> 00:38:27,310
I'm doing well.

569
00:38:27,410 --> 00:38:29,570
What about you two? Are you doing well?

570
00:38:29,870 --> 00:38:31,140
I'm doing just fine.

571
00:38:31,260 --> 00:38:32,610
But there's someone here,

572
00:38:32,640 --> 00:38:35,170
and I'm not sure how he’s doing.

573
00:38:40,100 --> 00:38:40,970
Sarm...

574
00:38:41,580 --> 00:38:42,580
Are you doing well?

575
00:38:48,430 --> 00:38:49,710
And what about you, PiMai?

576
00:38:50,310 --> 00:38:51,690
How's your shop holding up?

577
00:38:52,050 --> 00:38:53,050
It's doing alright.

578
00:38:53,440 --> 00:38:54,130
Oh!

579
00:38:54,420 --> 00:38:56,690
I made desserts for you two, actually.

580
00:38:56,730 --> 00:38:57,390
Whoa.

581
00:38:57,460 --> 00:38:58,400
Can't wait to try them.

582
00:38:58,440 --> 00:38:59,200
Are you for real?

583
00:38:59,230 --> 00:38:59,810
PiMai.

584
00:39:00,050 --> 00:39:01,210
How about you open your dessert shop here?

585
00:39:01,380 --> 00:39:02,330
I'll buy them all every day.

586
00:39:02,670 --> 00:39:03,290
I'm serious.

587
00:39:03,320 --> 00:39:05,210
Hold your horses, Sarm.

588
00:39:05,320 --> 00:39:06,090
PiMai

589
00:39:06,120 --> 00:39:07,500
is about to open another branch.

590
00:39:07,530 --> 00:39:09,110
It's near his husband's place.

591
00:39:09,140 --> 00:39:10,550
Oh, really?

592
00:39:10,710 --> 00:39:11,670
For real?

593
00:39:14,030 --> 00:39:14,730
Oh.

594
00:39:14,850 --> 00:39:15,500
And...

595
00:39:16,330 --> 00:39:17,610
what about the Chiang Mai branch?

596
00:39:18,700 --> 00:39:19,500
You're

597
00:39:19,610 --> 00:39:20,910
leaving Chiang Mai?

598
00:39:22,310 --> 00:39:23,630
I'll still be in Chiang Mai.

599
00:39:23,900 --> 00:39:25,210
As for expanding,

600
00:39:25,250 --> 00:39:26,740
I just talked to Sib.

601
00:39:26,770 --> 00:39:28,130
We haven't agreed on anything yet.

602
00:39:28,450 --> 00:39:29,290
Aha.

603
00:39:30,710 --> 00:39:32,810
Living there alone,
has anyone tried to hit on you?

604
00:39:33,420 --> 00:39:34,210
I'm just

605
00:39:34,250 --> 00:39:35,810
protective of my little brother, you know.

606
00:39:35,840 --> 00:39:37,350
You live far away, too.

607
00:39:37,370 --> 00:39:39,110
Gosh, Sarm.

608
00:39:39,640 --> 00:39:40,910
There's only one

609
00:39:41,020 --> 00:39:42,120
who's been seeing him, no?

610
00:39:42,520 --> 00:39:44,170
Without fail, right?

611
00:39:45,410 --> 00:39:46,100
Hey.

612
00:39:46,160 --> 00:39:47,010
If he comes to see you

613
00:39:47,090 --> 00:39:47,850
empty-handed,

614
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:48,610
send him back.

615
00:39:50,870 --> 00:39:52,620
He doesn't come empty-handed, of course.

616
00:39:52,660 --> 00:39:55,260
Recently,
he even offered to be his sponsor,

617
00:39:55,290 --> 00:39:56,490
buying him a mall
so he can open a shop.

618
00:39:56,620 --> 00:39:58,390
- Whoa.
- So over-the-top.

619
00:39:58,450 --> 00:39:59,450
Though I heard

620
00:39:59,570 --> 00:40:01,410
this guy's got quite a mouth on him.

621
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:03,650
Like he's got
a whole pack of dogs in his mouth.

622
00:40:04,060 --> 00:40:04,810
It's true.

623
00:40:05,180 --> 00:40:05,830
PiMai.

624
00:40:06,120 --> 00:40:07,330
Don't give in so easily, okay?

625
00:40:07,370 --> 00:40:08,810
You need to stay strong, you know?

626
00:40:09,420 --> 00:40:10,330
Understood?

627
00:40:10,800 --> 00:40:11,830
Next time,

628
00:40:11,890 --> 00:40:13,410
he'll know better than to mess with you.

629
00:40:13,510 --> 00:40:14,930
How tough do I have to be, Sarm?

630
00:40:14,970 --> 00:40:15,890
Whoa.

631
00:40:15,930 --> 00:40:16,850
Make sure he learns his lesson.

632
00:40:18,420 --> 00:40:19,030
I'm telling you,

633
00:40:19,060 --> 00:40:20,060
even if he comes crawling on his knees,

634
00:40:20,130 --> 00:40:21,340
begging and pleading,

635
00:40:21,670 --> 00:40:22,810
don't listen to him.

636
00:40:23,570 --> 00:40:24,400
Understood?

637
00:40:24,430 --> 00:40:25,110
Gosh.

638
00:40:25,150 --> 00:40:27,090
You just love stirring him up,
don't you, Sarm?

639
00:40:27,130 --> 00:40:28,160
Let me pray that

640
00:40:28,550 --> 00:40:30,090
everything you wish upon him

641
00:40:30,130 --> 00:40:31,930
comes right back to you.

642
00:40:31,970 --> 00:40:32,890
Sadhu.

643
00:40:33,230 --> 00:40:34,010
Wait.

644
00:40:34,290 --> 00:40:35,210
This kind of thing

645
00:40:35,390 --> 00:40:36,920
will never happen to me.

646
00:40:38,820 --> 00:40:39,300
Hey.

647
00:40:39,330 --> 00:40:40,130
Let's take some photos

648
00:40:40,210 --> 00:40:41,410
to remember this by.

649
00:40:44,060 --> 00:40:45,290
Three, two, one.

650
00:40:45,690 --> 00:40:46,580
Let's go rapid-fire.

651
00:41:18,970 --> 00:41:20,030
What is this?!

652
00:41:20,610 --> 00:41:22,290
Why are you all staring at me?

653
00:41:22,320 --> 00:41:23,250
I don't like this at all.

654
00:41:23,290 --> 00:41:25,000
I've only got one pimple.

655
00:41:25,400 --> 00:41:26,730
I thought it was a boil.

656
00:41:27,040 --> 00:41:28,440
It looked just like one.

657
00:41:28,880 --> 00:41:31,080
- So where have you been these past six months,
- Dad.

658
00:41:31,120 --> 00:41:31,800
huh?

659
00:41:31,840 --> 00:41:32,360
Listen.

660
00:41:32,610 --> 00:41:34,030
Here's the story.

661
00:41:34,260 --> 00:41:35,370
This whole time,

662
00:41:35,490 --> 00:41:36,720
I was just tripping.

663
00:41:36,750 --> 00:41:37,810
But right now,

664
00:41:37,900 --> 00:41:38,980
I'm back.

665
00:41:39,320 --> 00:41:40,520
Good as new.

666
00:41:41,010 --> 00:41:42,290
I'm now 100 percent clean.

667
00:41:42,430 --> 00:41:43,430
From now on,

668
00:41:43,600 --> 00:41:45,090
whatever I've caused,

669
00:41:45,190 --> 00:41:46,580
whatever problems have happened,

670
00:41:46,660 --> 00:41:47,570
whether it's system issues,

671
00:41:47,600 --> 00:41:48,500
financial losses,

672
00:41:48,530 --> 00:41:49,330
or the business going under,

673
00:41:49,760 --> 00:41:50,790
I'll take responsibility.

674
00:41:52,210 --> 00:41:52,730
Oh.

675
00:41:52,980 --> 00:41:54,080
And let me tell you,

676
00:41:54,430 --> 00:41:56,000
I won't take long.

677
00:42:12,490 --> 00:42:13,400
Dad!

678
00:42:13,610 --> 00:42:14,570
I'm sorry.

679
00:42:14,740 --> 00:42:16,050
I'm sorry for neglecting my work

680
00:42:16,160 --> 00:42:17,530
and being irresponsible.

681
00:42:17,630 --> 00:42:18,330
Dad!

682
00:42:18,370 --> 00:42:20,120
- Wait, wait, wait.
- Dad, I'm really sorry!

683
00:42:20,150 --> 00:42:20,910
Hey.

684
00:42:20,950 --> 00:42:21,530
Yes?

685
00:42:21,570 --> 00:42:22,700
When you vanished

686
00:42:22,730 --> 00:42:24,310
and we couldn't reach you,

687
00:42:24,990 --> 00:42:27,450
do you have any idea
how worried your family was, huh?

688
00:42:27,990 --> 00:42:30,020
Oh, I made everyone worry about me?

689
00:42:30,060 --> 00:42:30,890
I'm sorry, Dad.

690
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:33,920
Dad...

691
00:42:37,080 --> 00:42:38,200
You've got a pimple, too.

692
00:42:38,330 --> 00:42:38,760
See?

693
00:42:38,800 --> 00:42:39,310
Where?

694
00:42:39,340 --> 00:42:40,990
Here. Let me pop it.

695
00:42:43,730 --> 00:42:44,980
- Oh, wait!
- Mm.

696
00:42:45,340 --> 00:42:46,250
I love you, Dad.

697
00:42:46,280 --> 00:42:47,960
Gosh, you win.

698
00:42:48,310 --> 00:42:49,910
You can go wherever you want.

699
00:42:49,940 --> 00:42:50,720
- Go ahead.
- Oh, Dad.

700
00:42:50,750 --> 00:42:51,650
I've got something for you.

701
00:42:53,220 --> 00:42:54,050
I love you.

702
00:42:54,670 --> 00:42:55,670
Love you.

703
00:42:57,130 --> 00:42:58,690
Gosh, just give me one already.

704
00:43:00,570 --> 00:43:02,300
Right, right, right.

705
00:43:07,890 --> 00:43:08,580
My man.

706
00:43:08,850 --> 00:43:09,680
Hey, my man.

707
00:43:10,000 --> 00:43:11,530
I'm truly grateful to you

708
00:43:11,960 --> 00:43:13,690
for bringing good things into my life.

709
00:43:16,020 --> 00:43:17,900
I really appreciate it. Thank you.

710
00:43:28,470 --> 00:43:29,230
Thank you.

711
00:43:35,380 --> 00:43:36,180
Hey!

712
00:43:37,010 --> 00:43:37,710
Sit down.

713
00:43:38,010 --> 00:43:38,690
What?

714
00:43:39,600 --> 00:43:40,990
I already kissed you all.

715
00:43:41,030 --> 00:43:41,780
There's...

716
00:43:42,080 --> 00:43:43,130
one left.

717
00:43:43,710 --> 00:43:44,710
That one.

718
00:43:48,860 --> 00:43:50,480
- Song. Come here already.
- Don't you dare.

719
00:43:50,520 --> 00:43:51,910
- Stay the hell away.
- Come here, Song.

720
00:44:15,660 --> 00:44:17,780
Don't bring shame to your father's name.

721
00:44:18,050 --> 00:44:18,910
Hm.

722
00:44:19,010 --> 00:44:20,500
Then I won't hold back.

723
00:44:20,810 --> 00:44:21,290
Go.

724
00:44:35,020 --> 00:44:36,020
Nim!

725
00:44:36,920 --> 00:44:38,310
Yes?

726
00:44:40,440 --> 00:44:41,890
I'm on cloud nine.

727
00:45:25,010 --> 00:45:26,730
Mr. Sarm...

728
00:45:40,690 --> 00:45:41,530
Mr. Sarm!

729
00:45:43,440 --> 00:45:44,440
This man is now

730
00:45:45,820 --> 00:45:46,710
right in front of you.

731
00:45:53,200 --> 00:45:54,200
Hey! Get back.

732
00:45:54,930 --> 00:45:55,580
Oh.

733
00:46:00,210 --> 00:46:00,930
Little Jam.

734
00:46:01,380 --> 00:46:02,890
Why did you do that to Little Sarm?

735
00:46:03,100 --> 00:46:03,690
Oh!

736
00:46:03,720 --> 00:46:04,730
This Little Sarm is hurt.

737
00:46:06,230 --> 00:46:07,850
Why cannot I do that?

738
00:46:09,940 --> 00:46:10,570
Wait.

739
00:46:11,090 --> 00:46:12,090
What about us?

740
00:46:12,160 --> 00:46:13,130
What is it?

741
00:46:13,360 --> 00:46:14,070
Let go.

742
00:46:14,280 --> 00:46:14,890
I am going home.

743
00:46:16,570 --> 00:46:17,900
But you're my spouse.

744
00:46:20,610 --> 00:46:22,420
Listen carefully, Mr. Sarm.

745
00:46:23,400 --> 00:46:26,700
If sleeping together means
we have to call each other spouses,

746
00:46:27,660 --> 00:46:29,130
then I probably have

747
00:46:29,170 --> 00:46:31,290
77 of them scattered across the provinces.

748
00:46:32,310 --> 00:46:33,420
You are just

749
00:46:34,420 --> 00:46:36,610
a Pak Chong branch spouse, that is all.

750
00:46:37,790 --> 00:46:38,500
Let go.

751
00:46:40,900 --> 00:46:41,710
Hey.

752
00:46:41,980 --> 00:46:42,560
If that's the case,

753
00:46:42,590 --> 00:46:43,930
divorce them all

754
00:46:44,250 --> 00:46:45,530
and let me be your only one.

755
00:46:46,520 --> 00:46:47,930
I must be your number one.

756
00:46:48,130 --> 00:46:49,130
Nothing less.

757
00:46:49,220 --> 00:46:50,420
Do you understand?

758
00:46:50,450 --> 00:46:51,370
Someone like you

759
00:46:51,590 --> 00:46:53,530
could only be my last choice.

760
00:46:54,550 --> 00:46:55,930
Why is that, you might ask?

761
00:46:56,510 --> 00:46:57,290
Because...

762
00:46:57,570 --> 00:46:58,280
you are not

763
00:46:58,610 --> 00:46:59,090
hot!

764
00:47:14,730 --> 00:47:16,210
Can you give me a second chance?

765
00:47:16,710 --> 00:47:17,410
This time,

766
00:47:17,440 --> 00:47:18,570
just request

767
00:47:18,680 --> 00:47:19,630
whatever position you want.

768
00:47:20,380 --> 00:47:21,570
A spinning back hook kick,

769
00:47:21,710 --> 00:47:22,890
a two-fist strike,

770
00:47:22,960 --> 00:47:24,030
or something else?

771
00:47:24,080 --> 00:47:25,010
Just tell me.

772
00:47:25,290 --> 00:47:26,290
I can do it all.

773
00:47:28,050 --> 00:47:28,700
Let's do it now.

774
00:47:28,730 --> 00:47:29,890
Hey! Stop it.

775
00:47:29,930 --> 00:47:31,090
Wait, wait, wait.

776
00:47:31,210 --> 00:47:32,570
You are insane!

777
00:47:33,030 --> 00:47:33,930
Hey, you...

778
00:47:36,410 --> 00:47:37,610
There will not be a next time.

779
00:47:38,210 --> 00:47:39,290
Do not dare pull that again.

780
00:47:40,060 --> 00:47:41,840
Good or bad, I'm still your spouse!

781
00:47:43,460 --> 00:47:44,800
A spouse, you say?

782
00:47:45,830 --> 00:47:47,900
This is a win-win for both of us.

783
00:47:48,450 --> 00:47:49,100
Ouch!

784
00:47:49,140 --> 00:47:49,760
Little Jam.

785
00:47:50,580 --> 00:47:51,240
Come here.

786
00:47:51,290 --> 00:47:52,060
Hey, you!

787
00:47:52,400 --> 00:47:52,970
Hey.

788
00:47:53,010 --> 00:47:53,490
What?

789
00:47:53,520 --> 00:47:54,100
It hurts.

790
00:47:54,400 --> 00:47:54,860
Oh.

791
00:47:55,050 --> 00:47:55,610
You're hurt...

792
00:47:56,630 --> 00:47:57,490
Where does it hurt, Little Jam?

793
00:47:57,530 --> 00:47:58,260
- It hurts.
- Where?

794
00:47:58,340 --> 00:47:58,920
I'm sorry.

795
00:47:59,040 --> 00:47:59,820
Oh, Little Jam.

796
00:48:00,430 --> 00:48:01,250
I'm so sorry.

797
00:48:01,410 --> 00:48:02,190
I didn't mean it.

798
00:48:02,220 --> 00:48:03,010
Where does it hurt?

799
00:48:03,450 --> 00:48:04,340
Where does it hurt? Ouch!

800
00:48:04,650 --> 00:48:05,180
Ow.

801
00:48:05,230 --> 00:48:05,970
Little Jam.

802
00:48:10,190 --> 00:48:10,980
Little Jam!

803
00:48:11,020 --> 00:48:11,730
You're gonna do this to me, huh?

804
00:48:18,730 --> 00:48:19,340
Fine!

805
00:48:19,380 --> 00:48:20,400
You're gonna do this to me, huh?

806
00:48:22,430 --> 00:48:24,210
To all security personnel,

807
00:48:24,650 --> 00:48:26,050
close all the entrances and exits.

808
00:48:26,100 --> 00:48:27,250
Tonight,

809
00:48:27,580 --> 00:48:29,010
no one shall leave.

810
00:48:29,110 --> 00:48:30,580
The cat is about to chase the mouse.

811
00:48:32,800 --> 00:48:34,040
Ready.

812
00:48:35,050 --> 00:48:36,020
Set.

813
00:48:36,050 --> 00:48:37,230
And...

814
00:48:37,550 --> 00:48:38,050
Go!

815
00:48:45,290 --> 00:48:48,700
The annual marathon is about to begin.

816
00:48:52,570 --> 00:48:53,450
Curse you, Sarm.

817
00:48:53,480 --> 00:48:54,970
You're going after God's favorite?

818
00:48:55,760 --> 00:48:57,610
You just live your life,

819
00:48:58,240 --> 00:49:00,530
and I will go back to living mine.

820
00:49:01,200 --> 00:49:02,430
I want you to learn

821
00:49:02,470 --> 00:49:04,190
everything about how things work here

822
00:49:04,230 --> 00:49:05,770
within three months.

823
00:49:10,420 --> 00:49:16,610
♫It seems like something's moving♫

824
00:49:16,690 --> 00:49:23,130
♫What's in my heart isn't too much, but I only♫

825
00:49:23,160 --> 00:49:27,350
♫I only wish you nothing but the best♫

826
00:49:27,390 --> 00:49:31,700
♫Hoping your smile will never fade♫

827
00:49:31,730 --> 00:49:36,520
♫That's all, for I don't wish
to take someone's place♫

828
00:49:36,580 --> 00:49:40,780
♫I'll simply be right here, always within reach♫

829
00:49:40,830 --> 00:49:45,280
♫Like a gentle breeze bringing you peace♫

830
00:49:45,340 --> 00:49:51,910
♫I'll stay right here by your side, always♫

831
00:49:58,750 --> 00:50:04,690
♫I'll stay right here by your side♫

832
00:50:05,750 --> 00:50:08,140
[Your Third Series]
